@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+---
+name: initialize
+description: Set up a Danus checkout for DeepSeek Harness on first use, or repair its local configuration. Use when runtime/.danus-initialized is absent, OPERATOR.md is blank, or the operator asks to initialize or reconfigure Danus.
+---
+
+# Initialize Danus for DeepSeek Harness
+
+Set up this checkout as a persistent Danus deployment. DeepSeek Harness is the main
+agent, worker runtime, verifier runtime, strategy transport, and authoring
+runtime. Provider authentication stays in DeepSeek Harness.
+
+## 1. Read the current state
+
+From the repository root, read `OPERATOR.md` and check the current git branch.
+Run the bootstrap when `runtime/dsh/node_modules/.bin/dsh` is absent. Then run:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/check-dsh.sh
+bash scripts/doctor.sh
+```
+
+Report the DeepSeek Harness version and the configured Danus provider/model.
+
+## 2. Ask for the durable choices
+
+Collect these choices from the operator:
+
+- how to address them and which language to use;
+- a git working branch, with `deploy/<operator-or-host>` as the suggested name;
+- the DeepSeek Harness provider/model for Danus roles, with
+  `deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash` as the suggested value;
+- the warning level for model spending or quota;
+- the usual worker roster, with `high:3,xhigh:4` as the suggested roster.
+
+Record `high` for ordinary workers and `max` for xhigh workers. These are the
+native reasoning-effort values exposed by the bundled DeepSeek adapter.
+
+## 3. Provision and verify
+
+Create the working branch when the checkout is on `main`. Copy
+`config/danus.env.example` to the gitignored `config/danus.env`, then record the
+chosen model and variants. Fill `OPERATOR.md` with the operator's choices.
+
+Run:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/bootstrap.sh
+bash scripts/services.sh up verify
+bash scripts/doctor.sh
+```
+
+The service command starts DeepSeek Harness Web, followed by the verify
+service. Confirm that both services belong to this checkout. Create
+`runtime/.danus-initialized` after these checks pass.
+Commit the tracked operator profile and related requested changes locally.
+Secrets and `runtime/` remain untracked.
+
+## 4. Hand off
+
+Summarize the selected provider/model, worker roster, verification service, and
+spending warning. Give the operator `http://127.0.0.1:<DSH_PORT>` and ask them to
+open the page. Ask for the mathematics problem. Mention that the
+operator can later place their papers in
+`.agents/skills/write-paper/style/anchors/` to guide paper style.
